{"abstract":[{"text":"Work with astronomical time and geographic observer locations.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Time and Observers","role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/TimeAndObservers"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Accurate time handling is fundamental to astronomy. AstronomyKit provides ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime"},{"type":"text","text":" for precise time representation and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Observer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for geographic locations."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Working with Time","anchor":"Working-with-Time","level":2},{"type":"heading","text":"Creating Times","anchor":"Creating-Times","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Current time","let now = AstroTime.now","","\/\/ From calendar components (in UTC)","let eclipse = AstroTime(year: 2024, month: 4, day: 8, hour: 18, minute: 15)","","\/\/ From Foundation Date","let time = AstroTime(Date())","","\/\/ From Julian days since J2000","let jd = AstroTime(ut: 9132.5)"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Time Arithmetic","anchor":"Time-Arithmetic","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let now = AstroTime.now","","\/\/ Add days or hours","let tomorrow = now.addingDays(1)","let nextHour = now.addingHours(1)","let lastWeek = now.addingDays(-7)","","\/\/ Compare times","if tomorrow > now {","    print(\"Tomorrow comes after now\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Converting to Date","anchor":"Converting-to-Date"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let time = AstroTime.now","let date: Date = time.date","","\/\/ Format for display","let formatter = DateFormatter()","formatter.dateStyle = .medium","formatter.timeStyle = .short","print(formatter.string(from: time.date))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Understanding UT vs TT","anchor":"Understanding-UT-vs-TT"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"AstroTime stores two time values internally:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Universal Time (UT)"}]},{"text":": Based on Earth’s rotation, used for rise\/set times","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Terrestrial Time (TT)"}]},{"text":": Uniform time scale, used for planetary orbits","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let time = AstroTime.now","print(\"UT: \\(time.universalTime)\")  \/\/ Days since J2000 noon (UTC)","print(\"TT: \\(time.terrestrialTime)\")  \/\/ Days since J2000 noon (TT)","","\/\/ Create from Terrestrial Time directly","let fromTT = AstroTime(tt: 9132.5)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The difference (ΔT) is automatically handled by AstronomyKit."}]},{"anchor":"Accepted-Range","text":"Accepted Range","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positions, states, distances, and the searches built on them accept a Terrestrial Time within 4,000 Julian years of J2000: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"abs(time.terrestrialTime) <= 1_461_000"},{"type":"text","text":" days, roughly the years −2000 to +6000. That is about the span over which the VSOP87 planetary theory claims validity. Outside it, and for a non-finite time, they throw "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstronomyError\/badTime","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Pluto accepts a narrower span, about the years −100 to +4100."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A calculation that samples nearby times can throw within a short distance of either edge: light-travel correction looks back up to a few hours, the Moon’s state vectors sample about a second either side, and searches step by days to years, sometimes backward before stepping forward. Creating an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AstroTime"},{"type":"text","text":" outside the range is not an error; only the calculations reject it."}]},{"anchor":"Delta-T-Models","text":"Delta T Models","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The difference between TT and UT (called ΔT) varies over time and is estimated using a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/DeltaTModel","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Every "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" carries its own "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime\/deltaTModel","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (defaulting to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/DeltaTModel\/observed","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a yearly table of IERS Earth-rotation values extrapolated beyond its last entry), with no process-global mutable state. Time arithmetic and event searches propagate the input time’s model automatically, so concurrent tasks can use different models safely."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Create a time using the JPL Horizons Delta T model","let jplTime = AstroTime(year: 2027, month: 6, day: 21, deltaT: .jplHorizons)","let nextDay = jplTime.addingDays(1)  \/\/ Also uses .jplHorizons","","\/\/ Current instant with an explicit model","let nowEM = AstroTime.now(deltaT: .espenakMeeus)","","\/\/ Year-based seasonal events with an explicit model","let seasons = try Seasons.forYear(2027, deltaT: .jplHorizons)","","\/\/ Query Delta T directly in seconds","let deltaT = DeltaTModel.observed.deltaT(universalTime: 0)  \/\/ Seconds at J2000"]},{"anchor":"Sidereal-Time","text":"Sidereal Time","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get the sidereal time at the prime meridian:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let sidereal = AstroTime.now.siderealTime","print(\"Greenwich Sidereal Time: \\(sidereal) hours\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calculate local sidereal time for any longitude:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7, longitude: -74.0)  \/\/ NYC","let lst = AstroTime.now.siderealTime(longitude: observer.longitude)","print(\"Local Sidereal Time: \\(lst) hours\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The result is in 0 up to, but not including, 24 hours for any finite longitude. An infinite or NaN longitude returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".nan"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Working-with-Observers","text":"Working with Observers","type":"heading","level":2},{"anchor":"Creating-Observers","text":"Creating Observers","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Basic location (sea level)","let seattle = Observer(latitude: 47.6062, longitude: -122.3321)","","\/\/ With height above sea level (meters)","let everest = Observer(","    latitude: 27.9881,","    longitude: 86.9250,","    height: 8848.86",")"]},{"anchor":"Coordinate-Conventions","text":"Coordinate Conventions","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Latitude"}]},{"text":": -90° (south) to +90° (north)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Longitude"}]},{"text":": -180° (west) to +180° (east)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Height"}]},{"text":": Meters above sea level","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Built-in-Locations","text":"Built-in Locations","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let greenwich = Observer.greenwich       \/\/ Royal Observatory","let primeMeridian = Observer.primeMeridian  \/\/ 0°, 0°"]},{"anchor":"Observer-Properties","text":"Observer Properties","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.0, longitude: -105.0, height: 1600)","","\/\/ Local gravity (accounts for latitude and altitude)","let gravity = observer.gravity  \/\/ m\/s²","","\/\/ Atmospheric conditions at this elevation","let atmosphere = try observer.atmosphere","print(\"Pressure: \\(atmosphere.pressure) mbar\")"]},{"anchor":"Observer-Vectors","text":"Observer Vectors","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get the observer’s position relative to Earth’s center:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let observer = Observer.greenwich","","\/\/ Position vector in AU","let position = try observer.vector(at: .now)","","\/\/ Full state (position and velocity)","let state = try observer.state(at: .now)","print(\"Position: \\(state.position)\")","print(\"Velocity: \\(state.velocity)\")"]},{"anchor":"Time-Zones","text":"Time Zones","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AstronomyKit works entirely in UTC. Convert to local time using Foundation:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["if let sunrise = try CelestialBody.sun.riseTime(after: .now, from: observer) {","    let formatter = DateFormatter()","    formatter.timeZone = TimeZone(identifier: \"America\/New_York\")","    formatter.timeStyle = .short","    print(\"Sunrise (local): \\(formatter.string(from: sunrise.date))\")","}"]},{"anchor":"Codable-Support","text":"Codable Support","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both types support "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" for persistence ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AstroTime"},{"type":"text","text":" encodes its Universal Time value and decodes using "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/DeltaTModel\/observed","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"):"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7, longitude: -74.0)","let data = try JSONEncoder().encode(observer)","","let time = AstroTime.now","let timeData = try JSONEncoder().encode(time)"]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/GettingStarted"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit\/timeandobservers"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"https://github.com/cosinekitty/astronomy":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Astronomy Engine","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","title":"Astronomy Engine","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","type":"link"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/DeltaTModel/observed":{"abstract":[{"text":"Observed Earth rotation (default).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/DeltaTModel\/observed","title":"DeltaTModel.observed","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/deltatmodel\/observed","type":"topic","